      en: "The Cascade Range in Canada extends about 1,100 km through British Columbia, part of the Pacific Ring of Fire formed by subduction of the Juan de Fuca Plate. The highest Canadian peak is Mount Garibaldi at 2,678 m, while the US section has Mount Rainier at 4,392 m. Annual precipitation can exceed 3,000 mm (118 in). The range features dense forests, extensive glaciers, and several active volcanoes. Key economic activities include forestry and tourism.",
